ol_execution_start\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_01a0f6b654c97436adea33cad0d6775c|fc_01a0f6b654c97436adea33cad0d6775c\",\"toolName\":\"read\",\"args\":{\"path\":\"/Users/user/work/delegate-11-models-doctor/docs/agents/domain.md\"}}","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":60,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_execution_start\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_01a0f6b6568d76599d5a277814d88a96|fc_01a0f6b6568d76599d5a277814d88a96\",\"toolName\":\"read\",\"args\":{\"path\":\"/Users/user/work/delegate-11-models-doctor/docs/agents/issue-tracker.md\"}}","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":61,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_execution_start\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_01a0f6b6584571148b2e98aeb64a4e86|fc_01a0f6b6584571148b2e98aeb64a4e86\",\"toolName\":\"bash\",\"args\":{\"command\":\"ls src/ tests/ config/ 2>&1; echo \\\"===\\\"; wc -l src/*.rs tests/*.rs src/bin/*.rs 2>&1\"}}","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":62,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_execution_update\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_01a0f6b6584571148b2e98aeb64a4e86|fc_01a0f6b6584571148b2e98aeb64a4e86\",\"toolName\":\"bash\",\"args\":{\"command\":\"ls src/ tests/ config/ 2>&1; echo \\\"===\\\"; wc -l src/*.rs tests/*.rs src/bin/*.rs 2>&1\"},\"partialResult\":{\"content\":[]}}","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":63,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_execution_end\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_01a0f6b6568d76599d5a277814d88a96|fc_01a0f6b6568d76599d5a277814d88a96\",\"toolName\":\"read\",\"result\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"# Issue tracker: GitHub\\n\\nIssues and specs live in GitHub Issues on this repo. Use `gh`; it infers the repo from the clone.\\n\\n- **Publish** (a spec, a ticket): `gh issue create`, multi-line body from a heredoc or `--body-file`.\\n- **Fetch a ticket**: `gh issue view <n> --comments`.\\n- **Labels**: the triage vocabulary is in `triage-labels.md`.\\n- **Triage covers issues only.** Pull requests here are the owner's own work and never enter the triage queue.\\n\\n## Wayfinding\\n\\n`/wayfinder` keeps a **map**: one issue labelled `wayfinder:map` holding Notes, Decisions so far, and Fog. Its tickets are child issues.\\n\\n- **Child ticket**: a GitHub sub-issue of the map, labelled `wayfinder:<research|prototype|grilling|task>`. Without sub-issues, list the child in a task list in the map body and open the child body wi [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":64,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_execution_end\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_01a0f6b654c97436adea33cad0d6775c|fc_01a0f6b654c97436adea33cad0d6775c\",\"toolName\":\"read\",\"result\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"# Domain docs\\n\\nThis repo is single-context: one `CONTEXT.md` (the glossary) and `docs/adr/` (decisions), both at the root. Both are created lazily by `/domain-modeling` once a term or decision is settled; until then they are absent, and that is expected.\\n\\nBefore exploring an area, read `CONTEXT.md` and the ADRs that touch it, when they exist.\\n\\n- **Glossary terms**: name domain concepts (in issue titles, proposals, hypotheses, test names) with the term `CONTEXT.md` defines. A concept the glossary lacks is either invented language to reconsider or a gap to note for `/domain-modeling`.\\n- **ADR conflicts**: when your output contradicts an ADR, say so explicitly, in the form _Contradicts ADR-NNNN (<title>), but worth reopening because…_\\n\"}]},\"isError\":false}","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":65,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_execution_update\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_01a0f6b6584571148b2e98aeb64a4e86|fc_01a0f6b6584571148b2e98aeb64a4e86\",\"toolName\":\"bash\",\"args\":{\"command\":\"ls src/ tests/ config/ 2>&1; echo \\\"===\\\"; wc -l src/*.rs tests/*.rs src/bin/*.rs 2>&1\"},\"partialResult\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"config/:\\nmodels.json\\n\\nsrc/:\\nbackends\\nbin\\ncapability.rs\\ncli.rs\\nconfig.rs\\ncursor_bin.rs\\n