h(job_id: &str) -> PathBuf {\\n    std::env::temp_dir()\\n        .join(\\\"cursor-delegate-jobs\\\")\\n        .join(format!(\\\"{job_id}.json\\\"))\\n}\\n\\npub struct FileStatusRecordWriter;\\n\\nimpl StatusRecordWriter for FileStatusRecordWriter {\\n    fn write(&self, job_id: &str, record: &PollResult) {\\n        let _ = write_atomic(&status_record_path(job_id), &json_compact(record));\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Write to a unique tmp sibling, then rename over `path`, so readers never see a partial file.\\nfn write_atomic(path: &Path, contents: &str) -> std::io::Result<()> {\\n    [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":51,"content":"{\"type\":\"message_start\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_01a0f6fac5ec72189cdc3e9dc37eb2f8|fc_01a0f6fac5ec72189cdc3e9dc37eb2f8\",\"toolName\":\"read\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"# Domain docs\\n\\nThis repo is single-context: one `CONTEXT.md` (the glossary) and `docs/adr/` (decisions), both at the root. Both are created lazily by `/domain-modeling` once a term or decision is settled; until then they are absent, and that is expected.\\n\\nBefore exploring an area, read `CONTEXT.md` and the ADRs that touch it, when they exist.\\n\\n- **Glossary terms**: name domain concepts (in issue titles, proposals, hypotheses, test names) with the term `CONTEXT.md` defines. A concept the glossary lacks is either invented language to reconsider or a gap to note for `/domain-modeling`.\\n- **ADR conflicts**: when your output contradicts an ADR, say so explicitly, in the form _Contradicts ADR-NNNN (<title>), but worth reopening because…_\\n\"}],\"isError\":false,\"timestamp\":1790850026687}}","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":52,"content":"{\"type\":\"message_end\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_01a0f6fac5ec72189cdc3e9dc37eb2f8|fc_01a0f6fac5ec72189cdc3e9dc37eb2f8\",\"toolName\":\"read\",\"content\":[{\"