ecord: &PollResult) {\\n        let _ = write_atomic(&status_record_path(job_id), &json_compact(record));\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Write to a unique tmp sibling, then rename over `path`, so readers never see a partial file.\\nfn write_atomic(path: &Path, contents: &str) -> std::io::R [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":56,"content":"{\"type\":\"message_end\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_01a0f6fac94a76da8b0850fb996ddae6|fc_01a0f6fac94a76da8b0850fb996ddae6\",\"toolName\":\"read\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"use crate::types::PollResult;\\nuse crate::util::{json_compact, random_uuid};\\nuse std::fs;\\nuse std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\\n\\npub trait StatusRecordWriter: Send + Sync {\\n    fn write(&self, job_id: &str, record: &PollResult);\\n}\\n\\npub fn status_record_path(job_id: &str) -> PathBuf {\\n    std::env::temp_dir()\\n        .join(\\\"cursor-delegate-jobs\\\")\\n        .join(format!(\\\"{job_id}.json\\\"))\\n}\\n\\npub struct FileStatusRecordWriter;\\n\\nimpl StatusRecordWriter for FileStatusRecordWriter {\\n    fn write(&self, job_id: &str, record: &PollResult) {\\n        let _ = write_atomic(&status_record_path(job_id), &json_compact(record));\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Write to a unique tmp sibling, then rename over `path`, so readers never see a partial file.\\nfn write_atomic(path: &Path, contents: &str) -> std::io::Res [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":57,"content":"{\"type\":\"message_start\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_01a0f6facaad70da9373713577b5da88|fc_01a0f6facaad70da9373713577b5da88\",\"toolName\":\"read\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"// Test seams are injected as `dyn Fn` fields, and the poll/dispatch results are short-lived\\n// values returned once per call.\\n#![allow(clippy::type_complexity, clippy::large_enum_variant)]\\n\\npub mod backends;\\np